# Build artifacts
/build/*
# Committed binaries (v6.1.0 — prior-major slot corrected cc3 → cc5):
# - cycc (Cyrius Computer Compiler) — current-major, v6.0.0 rename
#   of cc5. Tracked so CI / install bootstrap have a starting point.
# - cc5 — the PRIOR-major compiler (last v5.x, 5.11.69; renamed to
#   cycc at v6.0.0). Tracked as the one prior-major reference per the
#   "current + one prior-major" policy. NOT in the bootstrap chain
#   (seed = bootstrap/asm → cybs → cycc); it's a historical /
#   break-glass artifact. Drops at v7.0.0 (rotates to the last v6.x
#   cycc — same binary name, so the slot effectively retires).
# - cycc-native-aarch64 — the cycc binary built NATIVELY on aarch64
#   (via `cyrius pulsar`). Tracked because it's the one cross-bin that
#   can't be regenerated by cross-compiling: ARM hardware self-host
#   needs a binary that already runs on ARM. The other cross_bins
#   (cycc_aarch64, cycc_win in cyrius.cyml) are rebuilt on demand by
#   CI / install, so they stay ignored.
# cc3 (v4.x-era seed) was DROPPED at v6.1.0: at the v6.0.0 cut the
# prior-major slot should have rotated cc3 → cc5 but didn't, leaving
# cc3 as a stale prior-PRIOR. Corrected here — cc5 is the real
# previous-major compiler.
!/build/cycc
!/build/cc5
!/build/cycc-native-aarch64
# Ad-hoc cross-compiled outputs at repo root (regenerated on demand;
# see src/main_aarch64_macho.cyr header and scripts/mac-selfhost.sh).
/cycc_macho
/cycc_macho_b
/cycc_macho_b_unsigned
/cycc_macho_c

# Temporary files
/tmp/

# Core dumps
*.core

